    {
      "id": "60436e2b3fe2d2ea18eff21361f976f41ec5b856",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3609146761,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "[CMakeLists.txt](/uploads/38a05f3d8e42769e41737c80f86586ca/CMakeLists.txt)\n\n[lua.exe.manifest.in](/uploads/70c17f4beca53aa26f5cf0469349fcab/lua.exe.manifest.in)\n\n[lua.rc.in](/uploads/16f321f79eb9e6c315bb4ff3b6bd214e/lua.rc.in)\n\nThese files was used to build 5.0 using\n\n[README](/uploads/045974c33fb05c20019dc15eaed02f74/README) Whitout the patches",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-07-27T23:01:37.908Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-28T01:44:31.435Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 511575650,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 25943,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3609458142,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "So that manifest has the UTF-8 code page setting in the incorrect position (as previously in the wireshark manifests.) That means that fixing the Lua manifest was not required for it to pass our tests when used as a DLL inside Wireshark. A correct manifest might be needed, somehow, when running the lua.exe command line interpreter.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-07-28T01:44:31.394Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-28T01:44:31.394Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 511575650,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 25943,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3614226172,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> That means that fixing the Lua manifest was not required for it to pass our tests when used as a DLL inside Wireshark.\n\nMy guess would be that if we just used a build of the unmodified Lua interpreter library, shipping *shark with the \"code page\" knob turned to 65001 and welded in place would suffice to deal with #15118.\n\nThat may be sufficient for most if not all programs that link with the Lua interpreter library, including the \"lua\" command.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-07-28T20:46:06.326Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-28T20:46:06.326Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 511575650,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 25943,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "afc5e862c0883e1e6e375dbbf185416ebb69b793",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3609171592,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I fixed our manifest for Wireshark and related applications in !25929, and just used the existing Unicode package that you built in the previous version of the MR and the tests worked. I did not do anything else to Lua; I'm not sure if I need to.\n\nWould one of the consequences of \"force code page 65001\" be that Ordinary Boring Vanilla Lua would do just fine with UTF-8 pathnames, as that would result in `_open()` and company, which take code page strings as arguments, expecting UTF-8 strings, that being the encoding of the code page?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-07-27T23:14:32.581Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-27T23:14:32.581Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 511575650,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 25943,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "717c6dd5923f4649dbba6ea0fd2fe61eb63aef8d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3609225168,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yes, that is my understanding from https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/apps/design/globalizing/use-utf8-code-page and https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/sbscs/application-manifests#activeCodePage with the caveat that this is only guaranteed with Windows 10 version 1903 (May 2019 Update) and later. The most recent versions of Qt still support Windows 10 version 1809 (which is what Windows Server 2019 is based on), so we allow Wireshark to be installed on that version. We could decide fairly easily to enforce later Windows requirements on 5.0, and require people with Windows 10 ver 1809/Server 2019 to install 4.6, I suppose.\n\nThe lua manifest might be useful for ensuring that any lua.exe or other command line Lua tools we provide along with our libraries work similarly to when the library is loaded, so Lua developers don't get unexpected results if they test outside Wireshark.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-07-27T23:41:06.119Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-07-27T23:41:06.119Z",
